The attached image illustrates the local inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 in skeletal muscle 24 hours post-injection. The top row, representing Nano-11 with OVA, shows AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) co-localizing with Mac-2+ monocytes and MHCII+ cells (green), indicating efficient internalization by these immune cells. In contrast, the bottom row, representing soluble OVA, shows very few inflammatory cells and no significant red or green signals, highlighting Nano-11's role in recruiting and being phagocytized by monocytes and MHCII+ cells, a crucial step for antigen delivery and immune activation.